Description: avfilter/tonemapx: read the MMR weights of each piece from that piece's offset
 update_dovi_buf() packs the MMR weights of a component's pieces one
 after another, two rows of four floats for each order. It stores the
 row where each piece starts. Every code path of tonemapx adds that row
 number to a float pointer. So when a component has more than one MMR
 piece, each piece after the first read its weights from a quarter of
 its offset, inside the weights of the pieces before it.
 .
 With the previous patch, P and T reach their second and later pieces.
 On a synthetic profile 5 picture with P and T in two MMR pieces, 588 of
 705 checked patches came out more than one code from the definition,
 up to 166 luma and 469 chroma codes, on the C, SSE4.2, AVX2 and NEON
 paths. I in more than one MMR piece read the wrong weights in the same
 way before this series. tonemap_cuda counts in rows of four and was
 right.
 .
 Store the offset in floats.
